# No @notchip:registry mapping here on purpose — a scope registry in .npmrc
# hijacks EVERY scoped fetch/publish (npm view, npm publish, even with
# --registry flags, because scope config beats --registry). Publish routing
# comes from package.json publishConfig (npmjs) and CI's explicit
# --@notchip:registry flags in .github/workflows/publish.yml.
#
# No npmjs authToken here either — CI publishes to npmjs via OIDC trusted
# publishing (no token at all), and a ${NPM_TOKEN} line shadows ~/.npmrc for
# local publishes (an unset var makes npm publish fail with a misleading
# 404/401). Only GitHub Packages still authenticates via env token, in CI.
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GIT_PAT}
